#{[{:activity/_scope [{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116120} :activity/id #uuid "3b658871-23f8-5b8d-92ee-5294fec9bba3" :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116120 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116493 :tutorial/content "We can use Gaussian elimination to find the general solutions of systems with any number of equations and variables. For instance, consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y+z &=1, \\\\ y+3z &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThis system has the augmented matrix\n![](images/8a/8a8452587098eed9b697c3999c356359b949429f29ce16af2c81cf728be9480e.svg)\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\, & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+4z &=1 \\\\ y+3z &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe see that the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable $z.$ From the second equation, we get $y=-3z,$ and from the first equation, we obtain $x=1-4z.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=1-4z, \\\\ y &=-3z, \\\\ z &=z.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1-4z \\\\ -3z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+z\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "3eff050b-e4ba-52e5-aa10-7bba2feef2fc" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3162 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "6022e9b9-60ab-5ac5-b16a-17583fa649c3" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116121}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116121 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115241 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d81e3f1-d930-59ee-b439-2a3645aebb6c"} :step/id #uuid "79bb6bd1-8c36-5f56-9575-8a1b8388eb57" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116122}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116122 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116494 :tutorial/content "Recall that a system of linear equations is called **consistent** if it has at least one solution. Otherwise, if there are no solutions, the system is called **inconsistent**. \n\nFor a consistent system, \n\n- the system is called **consistent independent** if the solution is unique, while\n\n- the system is called **consistent dependent** if there are infinitely many solutions.\n\n![](images/f5/f5b808eac6e1d865b13b68ce2a4f7d317560ae3965928e478531fcd2148c2c6b.png)" :tutorial/id #uuid "e0c85152-daea-5a87-a3ba-81870558c7a2" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3163 :tutorial/title "Consistent and Inconsistent Systems of Linear Equations"} :step/id #uuid "2fa6eba1-6298-51b5-bbc9-bd8c46a79468" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116209}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116123 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115242 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "22733f71-de4a-5058-a41c-039e66e333c5"} :step/id #uuid "1d1a97f8-c872-5285-b963-d1938948df37"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116209 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115299 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9469d5c-e097-590c-8ddb-2c7fda353fac"} :step/id #uuid "e80cfcd9-1219-52d8-96c7-0ee06cdf52fc" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116123}}] :activity/title "Gaussian Elimination For NxM Systems of Equations" :activity/type {:db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186115479} {:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425950} :activity/id #uuid "080f971c-621c-5ccf-b883-b98c49745b79" :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425950 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425949 :question/id #uuid "db005b4e-86cd-5194-b2fd-10ca4ee59c03"} :step/id #uuid "2c3254d8-7342-5cba-aa85-c696386c710a" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425952}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425951 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115832 :question/id #uuid "e80c83a9-9107-528b-af57-73287d15e8e2"} :step/id #uuid "3b9e4957-843e-5d56-8704-c60e6e8f032c"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425952 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115831 :question/id #uuid "84cf8820-fa64-5d50-9d9c-d3a9404788a4"} :step/id #uuid "e9dff08f-68e1-5fe8-9586-d7f8edd2598c" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425951}}] :activity/title "Gaussian Elimination For NxM Systems of Equations" :activity/type {:db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425937} {:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492937} :activity/id #uuid "6e7bba4e-e339-5059-bc4b-363cbe14a29f" :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492937 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115830 :question/id #uuid "8cd9c6c5-780e-5f01-93cc-d5e9b9533129"} :step/id #uuid "2361ed3b-bfae-5a29-916a-e207bd92ed86" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492989}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492948 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492840 :question/id #uuid "22d64530-5ce7-515c-aafe-c528e2fc812f"} :step/id #uuid "49cc5d2d-b51f-5454-b5d2-2fecc8135eb1" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492950}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492950 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400646 :question/id #uuid "4890e1ff-ed9a-5558-acd1-bcef01439e04"} :step/id #uuid "4f6ca757-aec4-527a-86a3-ce82de0d867c" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492984}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492984 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492874 :question/id #uuid "7409a043-b196-5341-8318-5b111a0c527e"} :step/id #uuid "a93f2400-74e9-5bc9-a239-9a89e32c8532"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492989 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344961 :question/id #uuid "a0c28bd7-70de-59aa-93c9-933cbaca4593"} :step/id #uuid "b7e356b4-fa42-567c-864c-79ee57dd45e6" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492948}}] :activity/title "Gaussian Elimination For NxM Systems of Equations" :activity/type {:db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492210}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186048445 :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115241 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115070 :question/id #uuid "dc6dd9b4-de7f-52d0-8ff9-a7a7f7a9abd7" :question/math-academy-id "e-4711" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n![](images/40/406033f059dc4438ea55d43d2bd00b3b79bb99365a2e4846c995f4a447acfd82.svg)\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n![](images/be/bed2784d17ee63b805917b492052daa7ef079c1682bbc78468eb10f314a92b1f.svg)\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n![](images/91/91175ab97472067cd14ffff740bb3a98718436f1e94de7a4a6d7fdfb1b35b81f.svg)\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $z,$ and we have one free variable, $y.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $z$ in terms of $y.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-1-5y \\\\ y &=y \\\\ z &=3,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1-5y \\\\ y \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d81e3f1-d930-59ee-b439-2a3645aebb6c" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557573 :question-generator/id #uuid "d3ac02e4-4a1b-5e90-b15c-bf75d125145d" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186115241.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115751 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a25a6cc1-d88b-5f9f-aae1-cd3eb5867629" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113473} {:answer/id #uuid "b77df5f9-58e2-575f-bfdb-d097b57fc68f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}z \\\\ 13 - 2z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}, z ∈ (- ∞, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113474} {:answer/id #uuid "cee3daed-dbf4-59da-87b6-fc369d2242f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}z \\\\ 13 - 2z \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}, z ∈ (- ∞, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113475} {:answer/id #uuid "fc60f84e-4b0e-50e1-8012-0e75aaf5aef9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 13 - 2z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}, z ∈ (- ∞, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113476} {:answer/id #uuid "fe885f5c-7b1a-558b-a68d-cf982e4ed839" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 - z \\\\ 13 - 2z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}, z ∈ (- ∞, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113477}] :answer-field/id #uuid "83a4d783-f324-5167-b920-c6eb60540d44" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113472}] :question/id #uuid "d3d66d49-8ab9-5eb7-8d2f-d0c60a5c4d4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-32234" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n$\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x + y + 2z &=19 \\\\ 3x + y + 2z &=31\\end{aligned}\\right.$.\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115830 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "90d6f3fc-4b07-573d-909e-71ad76038bc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113918} {:answer/id #uuid "66d8f448-8728-5a93-9a65-75b7c8a60923" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2+3z \\\\ 2+3z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492423} {:answer/id #uuid "8de04b4a-cc0c-503c-b014-8f1ba934eb81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2-3z \\\\ 2+3z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492497} {:answer/id #uuid "977e4b58-8b63-5c8e-b09e-907ea3fc4715" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2-3z \\\\ 3z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492510} {:answer/id #uuid "b58da9b9-82d8-54d2-94d7-4d4f9a370f16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2-3z \\\\ 2-3z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492582}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2-3z \\\\ 2+3z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492497} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c202514-58b0-57fd-9d4a-d9d9f27c390e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113917}] :question/id #uuid "8cd9c6c5-780e-5f01-93cc-d5e9b9533129" :question/math-academy-id "q-42040" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+3z &=-2 \\\\ x+y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the standard method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now  \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+3z &=-2 \\\\ y-3z &=2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-2-3z \\\\ y &=2+3z \\\\ z &=z,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the latter can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2-3z \\\\ 2+3z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266111 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d6a91da-fd38-559c-b128-19dbc7c776d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263546} {:answer/id #uuid "a2aede61-88b5-5a76-9ec8-106c89064823" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3{x}_{3}+1 \\\\ 5{x}_{3}-1 \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264378} {:answer/id #uuid "c1490779-e503-5831-b724-e9dbf247059f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1-3{x}_{3} \\\\ 1-5{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264677} {:answer/id #uuid "ed2aed37-0c4b-5f9c-8951-b59ecdbcba2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3{x}_{3}+1 \\\\ 1-5{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265070} {:answer/id #uuid "ff176417-b95c-5350-be8a-fc42f217620b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3{x}_{3}-1 \\\\ 5{x}_{3}+1 \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265244}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3{x}_{3}+1 \\\\ 5{x}_{3}-1 \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264378} :answer-field/id #uuid "1999c267-61b7-5858-983a-df3e642d00c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265286}] :question/id #uuid "9e0a0a65-dec2-598f-90c5-c70695152a49" :question/math-academy-id "q-131715" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} &=2 \\\\ {x}_{1}-3{x}_{3} &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n \nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 & -1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe corresponding system is now  \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{3} &=1 \\\\ {x}_{2}-5{x}_{3} &=-1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2},$ and we have one free variable, ${x}_{3}.$ That means we need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ in terms of ${x}_{3}.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} &=3{x}_{3}+1 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=5{x}_{3}-1 \\\\ {x}_{3} &={x}_{3},\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{3}$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3{x}_{3}+1 \\\\ 5{x}_{3}-1 \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266112 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "150b8c63-cad2-507c-af99-2caf46c53ce7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5{x}_{3}-4 \\\\ 1-2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263196} {:answer/id #uuid "65da6370-1e54-53a6-8151-ac1ec3ef9e6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5{x}_{3}+4 \\\\ 2{x}_{3}+1 \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263881} {:answer/id #uuid "b5b758ce-eb9d-5dc8-85ff-c1262d0ecfc8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4-5{x}_{3} \\\\ 1-2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264574} {:answer/id #uuid "cc2515f8-96f9-59a1-9947-de1efbe1d2e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5{x}_{3}-4 \\\\ 2{x}_{3}-1 \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264787} {:answer/id #uuid "e6d4c49a-347d-549e-930b-1bad5d6bd1a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265011}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5{x}_{3}-4 \\\\ 1-2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263196} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c1fad65-c66c-5abb-b566-f399e550fab9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265356}] :question/id #uuid "175b6895-5ce4-52f4-b20c-0c4033601e3d" :question/math-academy-id "q-131717" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=-1 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2} &=3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n \nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -5 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -5 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}-3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -5 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe corresponding system is now  \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-5{x}_{3} &=-4 \\\\ {x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2},$ and we have one free variable, ${x}_{3}.$ That means we need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ in terms of ${x}_{3}.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} &=5{x}_{3}-4 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=1-2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3} &={x}_{3},\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{3}$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5{x}_{3}-4 \\\\ 1-2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302108 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16c59c60-7047-52d5-87e2-939004f4e5df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{y}{5}-2 \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300051} {:answer/id #uuid "2f11b4f8-857a-5c20-acad-ec6bae4a9637" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300189} {:answer/id #uuid "7456e911-694c-5708-b6ea-4413295c3756" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{5}{2}-y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300539} {:answer/id #uuid "a14ecff4-c49b-5d5d-a419-1378eddbc09c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5-y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300774} {:answer/id #uuid "aa051ba2-8988-5b2b-a5fb-1ce37c227a56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{5}{2}+x \\\\ x\\end{bmatrix},\\,x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300815}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{5}{2}-y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300539} :answer-field/id #uuid "ead03c74-07ea-57d9-9500-45e44f75354b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301973}] :question/id #uuid "cbdb5209-5ae6-5fea-a525-87f604e2410b" :question/math-academy-id "q-32244" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+2y &=5 \\\\ -10x-10y &=-25 \\\\ 8x+8y &=20.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 & 5 \\\\ -10 & -10 & -25 \\\\ 8 & 8 & 20\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 & 5 \\\\ -10 & -10 & -25 \\\\ 8 & 8 & 20\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ -10 & -10 & -25 \\\\ 8 & 8 & 20\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+10{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 8 & 20\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-8){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now  \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y &=\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x$ and we have one free variable, $y.$ That means we need to find $x$  in terms of $y.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=\\frac{5}{2}-y \\\\ y &=y,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{5}{2}-y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302193 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01e2124c-250c-5553-90ac-ad036367a54c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -4-2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299936} {:answer/id #uuid "1428c74d-a417-5a13-a349-88d508754aa1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ 6+{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{2}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300041} {:answer/id #uuid "16ebfa7c-e065-59dc-ac56-9ad2d722ea9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -6-2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300054} {:answer/id #uuid "46144e61-deb2-5eb2-93d9-1c9a051af1e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -6+{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300311} {:answer/id #uuid "ceb22f69-ba3e-510b-bac2-26a4175bcd5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ 6-2{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{2}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300994}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -6-2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300054} :answer-field/id #uuid "fcaee800-c02a-5f44-8ba8-6b7bcc06692e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302033}] :question/id #uuid "a1b8b6ae-30af-5f18-a21d-8dba558350b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-32517" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3} &=-4 \\\\ {x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} &=-6.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 & 4 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 & 4 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now   \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} &=4 \\\\ {x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} &=-6.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2},$ and we have one free variable, ${x}_{3}.$ Since we have that ${x}_{1}=4$,  we only need to find ${x}_{2}$ in terms of ${x}_{3}.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} &=4 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=-6-2{x}_{3},\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{3}$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -6-2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326924 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50f9b50f-35ed-5015-90a2-abcb73e7da04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2z \\\\ 4z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324637} {:answer/id #uuid "5aacb359-a752-57ee-91e8-49aab1c366a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1+2z \\\\ -3z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324720} {:answer/id #uuid "7904e155-741c-55db-ada4-37737e9bba13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2+4z \\\\ -3z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324977} {:answer/id #uuid "9a333b0e-0c9f-57ef-9a78-652e513b4226" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2+4z \\\\ 1-3z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325282} {:answer/id #uuid "e2e79639-3620-552d-af88-21e978591b1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1+4z \\\\ 3z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325961}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1+2z \\\\ -3z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324720} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ff1beeb-90d1-5401-997f-ae3e61dc47dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326353}] :question/id #uuid "a7ff9f1a-cb7f-5669-aa2d-6b7ae8d5b3bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-42041" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-4z &=2 \\\\ 4x+y-5z &=4.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -5 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -5 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -5 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2z &=1 \\\\ y+3z &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=1+2z \\\\ y &=-3z \\\\ z &=z,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1+2z \\\\ -3z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400625 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d174f1e-8230-59a5-b790-dfbaab4e9521" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400627} {:answer/id #uuid "244aab6d-90be-578a-8092-166a36c8c9ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4y-3 \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400628} {:answer/id #uuid "83dd970a-9032-5161-9210-85e901723065" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4y+3 \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400629} {:answer/id #uuid "8e7e3b2b-d1a1-5446-8ee4-32636f7b1b2e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4y-3 \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400630} {:answer/id #uuid "0e38c584-fc56-5df5-a079-f3072bdddfc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3-4y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400631}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4y-3 \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400628} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a4567f4-6572-5d9e-8018-4068c6812f07" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400626}] :question/id #uuid "b0feb9ee-8e97-5292-aff6-05655689f05b" :question/math-academy-id "q-131712" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+8y &=-6 \\\\ -4x-16y &=12 \\\\ 6x+24y &=-18.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 8 & -6 \\\\ -4 & -16 & 12 \\\\ 6 & 24 & -18\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 8 & -6 \\\\ -4 & -16 & 12 \\\\ 6 & 24 & -18\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & -3 \\\\ -4 & -16 & 12 \\\\ 6 & 24 & -18\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 24 & -18\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-6{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now  \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+4y &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x$ and we have one free variable, $y.$ That means we need to find $x$  in terms of $y.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-4y-3 \\\\ y &=y,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4y-3 \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402009 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c3ccae38-2121-52d3-adbe-774101358f5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-8-10{x}_{3} \\\\ 6+6{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402011} {:answer/id #uuid "bd1763ae-5fcd-5d4b-b18a-af3a643749d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}8-{x}_{3} \\\\ 3+3{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402012} {:answer/id #uuid "300bc792-b634-5ba3-8561-858fdf7d8d69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-8-8{x}_{3} \\\\ 6-6{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402013} {:answer/id #uuid "55911223-4948-5180-95bf-96b38f95603a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-8-6{x}_{3} \\\\ 10+6{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402014} {:answer/id #uuid "e5a39045-c764-56cd-a094-6caa0b024ef0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-8-{x}_{3} \\\\ 6+{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402015}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-8-10{x}_{3} \\\\ 6+6{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402011} :answer-field/id #uuid "94d6271a-24bd-58c0-9553-83b2dc10742e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402010}] :question/id #uuid "f65d67ed-b94b-50cc-87d4-9aa7130f7547" :question/math-academy-id "q-32247" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} &=4 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} &=-2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n \nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -3 & -2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -3 & -2 & -2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -6 & 6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 10 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -6 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe corresponding system is now  \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+10{x}_{3} &=-8 \\\\ {x}_{2}-6{x}_{3} &=6.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2},$ and we have one free variable, ${x}_{3}.$ That means we need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ in terms of ${x}_{3}.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} &=-8-10{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} &=6+6{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3} &={x}_{3},\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{3}$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-8-10{x}_{3} \\\\ 6+6{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402756 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e80e6ba-d53c-56a1-8f14-814656e252d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2-z \\\\ 0 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402758} {:answer/id #uuid "240d49db-221f-5c96-a2c7-752016dd8d06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1-z \\\\ 0 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402759} {:answer/id #uuid "c205ae90-dae6-5981-8476-c566174adf7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-z \\\\ z-1 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402760} {:answer/id #uuid "a7eb10d8-4da4-5dab-bc8c-4a003f7cebfb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ z-1 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402761} {:answer/id #uuid "c70e171e-d942-5f58-90b7-b6fb6a232836" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402762}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ z-1 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402761} :answer-field/id #uuid "0fa49e40-cb09-52a9-be51-216ec3f67938" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402757}] :question/id #uuid "013e11bb-39c0-595b-a244-03847638286f" :question/math-academy-id "q-42019" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y+2z &=2 \\\\ y-z &=-1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=0 \\\\ y-z &=-1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=0 \\\\ y &=z-1 \\\\ z &=z,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ z-1 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186417081 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46e61892-168f-50bc-9184-3087f0aa19c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2+z \\\\ -z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417072} {:answer/id #uuid "59f7a4dc-26a3-51be-9f66-57bb37e63b92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}z \\\\ 2z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417073} {:answer/id #uuid "5e341f4d-4527-53f0-a549-17a212c07c94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2+z \\\\ z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417075} {:answer/id #uuid "86d4df82-dbcb-5384-b53a-8ca94675a39a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2+z \\\\ 0 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417076} {:answer/id #uuid "b3937866-2599-550e-8d7d-230111af4c2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2+z \\\\ -2z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417077}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2+z \\\\ -2z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417077} :answer-field/id #uuid "40f01e87-54e2-5dd2-9850-20313302577b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417080}] :question/id #uuid "32425960-ceab-536a-8061-1f2469974e99" :question/math-academy-id "q-32220" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+z &=2 \\\\ y+2z &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-z &=2 \\\\ y+2z &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=2+z \\\\ y &=-2z \\\\ z &=z,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the latter can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2+z \\\\ -2z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557520 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16ccdedd-6990-5c9d-a5e7-669cb20766cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2w+6 \\\\ -3w+1 \\\\ w-3 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557509} {:answer/id #uuid "1eaab110-0c1d-58e2-a36a-75f81be4b961" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3w+1 \\\\ -2w+6 \\\\ w-3 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557511} {:answer/id #uuid "4d74f315-88b3-5c8a-b82e-0c35a568b22d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2w-6 \\\\ -3w+1 \\\\ w-3 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557527} {:answer/id #uuid "a82b5c6a-3d85-527b-907c-39a847d234d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2w+6 \\\\ -3w+1 \\\\ w-3 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557550} {:answer/id #uuid "f0b3d465-f8aa-56d0-aac9-e318dba0f152" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2w+6 \\\\ 1 \\\\ w-3 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557565}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2w+6 \\\\ -3w+1 \\\\ w-3 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557550} :answer-field/id #uuid "3df2332a-884a-5e30-9bff-9af78c8973ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557517}] :question/id #uuid "4149b33c-f03c-5dc8-a587-d4628af75acd" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-2y-4z+2w &=22 \\\\ 2x+y-z+8w &=16 \\\\ 2x+4w &=12.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}2 & -2 & -4 & 2 & 22 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1 & 8 & 16 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 12\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}2 & -2 & -4 & 2 & 22 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1 & 8 & 16 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 12\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -1 & -2 & 1 & 11 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1 & 8 & 16 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 12\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -1 & -2 & 1 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & 6 & -6 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 12\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -1 & -2 & 1 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & 6 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & 2 & -10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -1 & -2 & 1 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & 2 & -10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -1 & -2 & 1 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -2 & -6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -1 & -2 & 1 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1 & -3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -1 & -2 & 1 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1 & -3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(2){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -1 & 0 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1 & -3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1 & -3\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2w &=6 \\\\ y+3w &=1 \\\\ z-w &=-3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y$ and $z$, and we have one free variable, $w$. That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ and $z$ in terms of $w$.\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-2w+6 \\\\ y &=-3w+1 \\\\ z &=w-3 \\\\ w &=w,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $w$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2w+6 \\\\ -3w+1 \\\\ w-3 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557532 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bf4863e-3812-5163-be18-589b2a9762b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2w-2 \\\\ -w-5 \\\\ -w+6 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557515} {:answer/id #uuid "4438ccf8-0cf2-5b16-8b50-a324fa882d86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2w+2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -w+6 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557522} {:answer/id #uuid "85ef319c-cf8c-51bd-b6a9-a076f2220193" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-w-5 \\\\ -2w+2 \\\\ -w+6 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557534} {:answer/id #uuid "92a3c94b-a6d0-5d86-a0b4-141b13c2745e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2w+2 \\\\ -w-5 \\\\ -w+6 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557539} {:answer/id #uuid "f2471b96-19e0-554d-9c47-9690ecd4e85f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2w+2 \\\\ -w-5 \\\\ -w+6 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557566}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2w+2 \\\\ -w-5 \\\\ -w+6 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557566} :answer-field/id #uuid "10d4ff0b-a1ed-57e4-bbde-79ee3d0faaa8" :answ