is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-z &=-6 \\\\ y+3z &=-2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y$, and we have one free variable, $z$. That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z$.\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=z-6 \\\\ y &=-3z-2 \\\\ z &=z,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}z-6 \\\\ -3z-2 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557551 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4fa00707-ca62-5e26-8cd5-1f7625b9c10c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4z+2 \\\\ -3z-5 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557528} {:answer/id #uuid "995676a6-2cf6-5858-b738-aba60a8aeefa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4z+2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557541} {:answer/id #uuid "9cedd0e2-f0fe-57de-8bf9-74b0d6aeefe1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4z-2 \\\\ -3z-5 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557542} {:answer/id #uuid "d32535a8-e248-5a18-9233-6d41ff79b84a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3z-5 \\\\ -4z+2 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557560} {:answer/id #uuid "d7b08673-f5a7-5468-88d2-82fface9dd69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4z+2 \\\\ -3z-5 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557561}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4z+2 \\\\ -3z-5 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557528} :answer-field/id #uuid "32299d3b-6034-5ff8-afd5-342220d2ad49" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557513}] :question/id #uuid "adb0568a-cc33-548d-9e70-7aec30b5b6bd" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+2y+14z &=-6 \\\\ x+4y+16z &=-18 \\\\ -2x-4y-20z &=16.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 2 & 14 & -6 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 16 & -18 \\\\ -2 & -4 & -20 & 16\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 2 & 14 & -6 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 16 & -18 \\\\ -2 & -4 & -20 & 16\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 16 & -18 \\\\ -2 & -4 & -20 & 16\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 9 & -15 \\\\ -2 & -4 & -20 & 16\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ -2 & -4 & -20 & 16\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -6 & 10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+4z &=2 \\\\ y+3z &=-5.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y$, and we have one free variable, $z$. That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z$.\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-4z+2 \\\\ y &=-3z-5 \\\\ z &=z,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4z+2 \\\\ -3z-5 \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557557 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11f75aad-535e-5349-ac30-0817cbc6131e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2w-2 \\\\ -w-6 \\\\ 3w-3 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557507} {:answer/id #uuid "67b5aba3-9287-5655-a310-8b430569b715" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2w-2 \\\\ -w-6 \\\\ 3w-3 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557531} {:answer/id #uuid "85f5e298-78dd-5de5-b5f3-f4c5ec30a051" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2w-2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 3w-3 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557535} {:answer/id #uuid "a0cb117c-63e0-5b48-8734-1e48dee2c005" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-w-6 \\\\ 2w-2 \\\\ 3w-3 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557545} {:answer/id #uuid "f8bddcd4-51ea-5bca-9efc-633ffe6faec6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2w+2 \\\\ -w-6 \\\\ 3w-3 \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix},\\,w\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 175921