 the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ -6 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n- Since $A$ is lower-triangular, the eigenvalues are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=-3\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=2.\n$$\n\n- Let's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors.\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=-3,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{1}I=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 0\\end{bmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=2,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{2}I=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ -6 & -5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nNow, we write down the general solution to the given linear system of differential equations: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-3t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302381 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44c3eef4-ad8c-522c-bbcd-cf09e489894c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-4t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300304} {:answer/id #uuid "7960167d-ad50-55a5-9bdc-d155e584b0d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t},\\,{c}_{1}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300561} {:answer/id #uuid "848b7ae4-f283-5a02-a755-8a4a09e0924c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-4t},\\,{c}_{1},\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300622} {:answer/id #uuid "e1b87a3e-5f6c-50c3-81c3-ad45363df7cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=