ix}.$\n\n- We are given that the eigenvalues are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=-1\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=2.\n$$\n\n- Let's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors.\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=-1,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{1}I=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=2,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{2}I=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -4\\end{bmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nNow, we write down the general solution to the given linear system of differential equations: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413716 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ec56082-7fc8-5f94-b44a-5cb5efe5d2d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{4t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413702} {:answer/id #uuid "54af6a24-5d99-5408-a766-dca48f108865" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413705} {:answer/id #uuid "8da94f97-391c-5f2d-9aa6-f93861ebaae3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413707} {:answer/id #uuid "9e8389b0-350f-5b8b-8932-a02eeebefaa4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413709} {:answer/id #uuid "b8299918-b9e8-5cbd-b68a-28bb2aaef1f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{4t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413710}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413709} :answer-field/id #uuid "d472becc-17da-5ab2-96b6-76c458eb3ce3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413713}] :question/id #uuid "b90d6d2e-cbeb-5361-979a-20fa4635915b" :question/math-academy-id "q-327993" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the system of differential equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &=4{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &=2{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n*Hint: The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=3$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=2.$*" :question/worked-solution "We need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n- We are given that the eigenvalues are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=3\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=2.\n$$\n\n- Let's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors.\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=3,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{1}I=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=2,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{2}I=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nNow, we write down the general solution to the given linear system of differential equations: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a Linear System of Differential Equations"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129307 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128951 :question/id #uuid "b0707ce1-a0fe-5749-9742-4768621332a1" :question/math-academy-id "e-5605" :question/problem "Find the substitution that will decouple the following system of differential equations: \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &=-3{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &=-3{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's construct the matrix differential equation $\\mathbf{x}'(t)=A\\mathbf{x}(t)$ for the given system:\n![](images/b1/b121e46eacd73987eb2d088f4b3904d293e267dd3a005cced0bfd85f55c5b300.svg)\n\nWe need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A.$\n\n- Since $A$ is lower-triangular, the eigenvalues are \n\n$$\n\\lambda_1=-3\n\\qquad\\text{and}\\qquad\n\\lambda_2=1.\n$$\n\n- Let's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors.\n\n- For $\\lambda_1 =-3,$ we get \n![](images/b9/b97a40ce65d174e23907ba00478f49f633ce1b2bf9fcb5fa3fb7627ed1e27d11.svg)\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n![](images/a2/a27de99267f5b34b0202c43b984c199264fd2b4808add80c2856bed984ab14f0.svg)\n\n- For $\\lambda_2 =1,$ we get \n![](images/61/61d0d2e59d71dfc71df3bb0604165a54d52fc483196bd452a03a02cb33d0d9e3.svg)\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n![](images/1a/1acdb041f910f83f6cd7d17194e8ce25bc7e82020b55559ff5889b71e052a4c0.svg)\n\nTherefore, we have ![](images/b5/b50817ce9b7984b26e5099dfab0a6205dec82ff90d7069a87901dc92098ec905.svg)\n\nFinally, the change of variables that decouples the system is given by $\\mathbf{x}(t) = E\\mathbf{u}(t),$ or equivalently,\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) &=4{u}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) &=3{u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2a962d5e-5cc9-530e-9f95-85c399af7e4b" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129581 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a797ac7-33c4-512f-90f8-59eb16783f56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) &={u}_{1}(t)-2{u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) &=3{u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402030} {:answer/id #uuid "54d062ef-f5a7-554f-9aec-32b3e4d45203" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) &={u}_{1}(t)-{u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) &=-{u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402031} {:answer/id #uuid "a9817443-5f2f-5697-b9b4-facc30ec893f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) &={u}_{1}(t)-{u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) &={u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402032} {:answer/id #uuid "bb06d79b-0719-5c04-a4f5-69705749bb3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) &=2{u}_{1}(t)-{u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) &=2{u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402033} {:answer/id #uuid "a0f2d3e6-cd5c-5ab7-a220-8d6563dfe260" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) &={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) &={u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402034}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) &={u}_{1}(t)-{u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) &={u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402032} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6c339bd-cf81-5ede-a22f-a63cc71054fd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402029}] :question/id #uuid "5c347aa2-fe8e-5437-94e5-a44fd44640d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-324455" :question/problem "Find the substitution that will decouple the following system of differential equations: \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &=3{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &={x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n- Since $A$ is upper-triangular, the eigenvalues are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=3\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=1.\n$$\n\n- Let's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors.\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=3,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{1}I=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=1,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{2}I=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nTherefore, we have $E=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nFinally, the change of variables that decouples the system is given by $x(t)=Eu(t)$, or equivalently,\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) &={u}_{1}(t)-{u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) &={u}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129710 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04bcc08f-6df3-5da3-a584-9f0a56dba8f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413697} {:answer/id #uuid "054c9cf6-e5e5-5a1d-822d-f6804209660e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -4 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413698} {:answer/id #uuid "309d74bd-887c-5635-863d-c7f4529c284e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413700} {:answer/id #uuid "33fd177f-44ac-5b25-b4d6-ccf693b7ba07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413701} {:answer/id #uuid "536f5988-b95f-5a22-8bfe-686e8a9dd306" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413704}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413701} :answer-field/id #uuid "87b3fc9a-3397-5555-bc9f-987194333d19" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413712}] :question/id #uuid "30504f26-ffc2-5a3c-bc4c-1549ba4e1d3f" :question/math-academy-id "q-39052" :question/problem "Let ${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}$ and ${v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}$ be eigenvectors of a matrix $A.$ Find the decoupling matrix of the differential equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we construct the matrix $E$, whose columns are the eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}:$\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, the decoupling matrix can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & ={E}^{-1} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot (-3)-2\\cdot (-4)}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302385 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05baeea3-d728-50f5-b72d-e465401c40fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) &=-{u}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) &={u}_{1}(t)-{u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299959} {:answer/id #uuid "0f431ed1-6f40-536e-a3ad-97fa488d66f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) &={u}_{1}(t)-{u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) &=-{u}_{1}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300019} {:answer/id #uuid "1021ee26-f6f3-52eb-9120-51a385d34e85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) &={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) &={u}_{1}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300026} {:answer/id #uuid "83ccab21-c662-531d-8f69-f322926b0931" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) &=-{u}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) &={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300617} {:answer/id #uuid "cfd17b9a-b8dc-5741-b6a6-061f0f548e5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) &=-{u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) &={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300999}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) &=-{u}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) &={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300617} :answer-field/id #uuid "16ac5a90-c924-561b-8c66-bde13a3fd48c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301301}] :question/id #uuid "3e7b2942-ef73-54dc-bbb9-2edab71c8980" :question/math-academy-id "q-327995" :question/problem "Find the substitution that will decouple the following system of differential equations: \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &=2{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &=-3{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n- Since $A$ is lower-triangular, the eigenvalues are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=2\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-1.\n$$\n\n- Let's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors.\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=2,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{1}I=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -3\\end{bmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=-1,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{2}I=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nTherefore, we have $E=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nFinally, the change of variables that decouples the system is given by $x(t)=Eu(t)$, or equivalently,\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) &=-{u}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) &={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302387 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f38fcfc-44df-570d-90c6-a2ccbda1b2c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) &=-{u}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) &={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300110} {:answer/id #uuid "4a1f2066-5bf3-5a7b-b6a2-70ed4de42133" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) &=-{u}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) &={u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300340} {:answer/id #uuid "9c97ffc4-319c-5e93-ac43-43f4c0d5d6de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) &=-{u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) &={u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300750} {:answer/id #uuid "cca74972-d379-517c-b3f7-9868a00c08d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) &={u}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) &={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300984} {:answer/id #uuid "fdf094b7-0a41-5fef-992e-b5e876ead7ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) &={u}_{1}(t)-{u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) &={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301217}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) &=-{u}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) &={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300110} :answer-field/id #uuid "42f44c0e-8d8b-5c4a-90ba-6b12239c6f47" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301453}] :question/id #uuid "29472cdb-94de-5b9d-aed0-3446bb6f052e" :question/math-academy-id "q-327997" :question/problem "Find the substitution that will decouple the following system of differential equations: \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &={x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &=-2{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n- Since $A$ is lower-triangular, the eigenvalues are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=1\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-1.\n$$\n\n- Let's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors.\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=1,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{1}I=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=-1,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{2}I=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nTherefore, we have $E=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nFinally, the change of variables that decouples the system is given by $x(t)=Eu(t)$, or equivalently,\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) &=-{u}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) &={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302388 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e2c83db-a072-54a3-ae84-57a6c280cbb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) &=-{u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) &={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300008} {:answer/id #uuid "4a54974b-7455-54b0-ade3-1939e9f1100b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) &={u}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) &={u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300342} {:answer/id #uuid "4e988501-3076-56a5-91c9-9b0291b103f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) &={u}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) &=-{u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300372} {:answer/id #uuid "8188867c-8366-59e2-a95d-cd63f4e7a7e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) &={u}_{1}(t)-{u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) &={u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300605} {:answer/id #uuid "d0a546e7-5ba4-550a-8754-a5ba28fac386" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) &={u}_{1}(t)-{u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) &={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301003}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) &={u}_{1}(t)-{u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) &={u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300605} :answer-field/id #uuid "34918ba4-a618-5619-a950-7a3a27771306" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301393}] :question/id #uuid "2149f4e9-9859-5a10-b144-85d555bdaabc" :question/math-academy-id "q-327998" :question/problem "Find the substitution that will decouple the following system of differential equations: \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &={x}_{1}(t)-4{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &=5{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n- Since $A$ is upper-triangular, the eigenvalues are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=1\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=5.\n$$\n\n- Let's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors.\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=1,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{1}I=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=5,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{2}I=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nTherefore, we have $E=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nFinally, the change of variables that decouples the system is given by $x(t)=Eu(t)$, or equivalently,\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) &={u}_{1}(t)-{u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) &={u}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302389 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04548a1f-22a8-54df-8b51-2d7a78f6f5d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) &=-{u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) &={u}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299951} {:answer/id #uuid "2454ab07-d3c2-52f4-a0fb-9f465b3daa42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) &=-{u}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) &=-{u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300136} {:answer/id #uuid "2a1a5903-275f-5a1e-80bc-4dd1462bc834" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) &=-{u}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) &={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300162} {:answer/id #uuid "d1879cde-aa6b-5dd1-8172-0d34d7934c1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) &={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) &={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301006} {:answer/id #uuid "debbbb97-e3cf-5118-b583-3289287906d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) &=-{u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) &={u}_{1}(t)-{u}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301067}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) &=-{u}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) &={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300162} :answer-field/id #uuid "0830b1a7-cfa9-5264-8d99-0c308154bd68" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301246}] :question/id #uuid "bde96fe6-6e2d-5275-8a67-e4ee0d456370" :question/math-academy-id "q-327999" :question/problem "Find the substitution that will decouple the following system of differential equations: \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &=-3{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &={x}_{1}(t)-2{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n- Since $A$ is lower-triangular, the eigenvalues are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=-3\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-2.\n$$\n\n- Let's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors.\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=-3,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{1}I=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=-2,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{2}I=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nTherefore, we have $E=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$ \n\nFinally, the change of variables that decouples the system is given by $x(t)=Eu(t)$, or equivalently,\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) &=-{u}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) &={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348262 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1adc7384-bf73-5c3c-98ad-997d99eb1d55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345585} {:answer/id #uuid "a3b47bd8-3a31-5e51-824e-de860b2954ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346772} {:answer/id #uuid "a7780c94-0db4-5568-86b1-0aa62f9eef04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346810} {:answer/id #uuid "d01a725f-75ed-588a-bd44-685560eac2b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347173} {:answer/id #uuid "e638786a-1d46-5074-8f58-2f73365791a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347380}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346772} :answer-field/id #uuid "794f51d6-4a96-5d26-a0f1-aa46daa5c8d6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347819}] :question/id #uuid "ebe46ab1-1508-593b-8a6b-0a0b98580178" :question/math-academy-id "q-79710" :question/problem "Let ${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$ and ${v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$ be eigenvectors of a matrix $A.$ Find the decoupling matrix of the differential equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we construct the matrix $E$, whose columns are the eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}:$\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, the decoupling matrix can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & ={E}^{-1} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot (-3)}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186392299 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95c071f2-d183-5d0d-884e-02458238551a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392301} {:answer/id #uuid "50375b4d-28b4-52c7-b4e8-da9e4abb9597" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392302} {:answer/id #uuid "d842ead4-dae7-578d-935a-cf5bac8c117d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392303} {:answer/id #uuid "f030fffb-a38d-5285-b3bf-8c22559708e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392304} {:answer/id #uuid "789eaf2b-dd8e-5756-a0fa-3809fed7c9da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392305}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392305} :answer-field/id #uuid "a618d060-9cdb-5241-8f90-2a9db5fbd04e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392300}] :question/id #uuid "547cf423-346c-5ea7-9462-268138005651" :question/math-academy-id "q-39699" :question/problem "Let ${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$ and ${v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$ be eigenvectors of a matrix $A.$ Find the decoupling matrix of the differential equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we construct the matrix $E$, whose columns are the eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}:$\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, the decoupling matrix can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & ={E}^{-1} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot (-2)}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186392306 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73910ac7-0fcb-5739-a4ef-ee62e3d20871" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392308} {:answer/id #uuid "def8d191-233e-58e5-a878-e67c318f4ee7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392309} {:answer/id #uuid "feae8b00-c727-56f2-ac19-3a222094595f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392310} {:answer/id #uuid "b2139fb4-d21d-588d-a1dd-7e43744c5df6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392311} {:answer/id #uuid "24669978-edf2-51af-8c8b-d2c608cd9695" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392312}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392308} :answer-field/id #uuid "b15a31f8-c915-5260-a280-5f4fee752c54" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392307}] :question/id #uuid "8820e364-7215-527a-af4b-9358606a911f" :question/math-academy-id "q-39705" :question/problem "Let ${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}$ and ${v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$ be eigenvectors of a matrix $A.$ Find the decoupling matrix of the differential equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we construct the matrix $E$, whose columns are the eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}:$\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, the decoupling matrix can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & ={E}^{-1} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 3-5\\cdot 1}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Decoupling Substitution of a Linear System of Differential Equations"}] :topic/math-academy-id 2087 :topic/title "Solving Homogeneous Systems of ODEs With Distinct Eigenvalues"}] [{:activity/_scope [{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088602} :activity/id #uuid "fd6a29fe-5312-5d49-b1ae-79d4178dc9eb" :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088602 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088928 :tutorial/content "Consider the function $f(x),$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x) = 2x+1.\n$$\n\nThis function $f$ takes a real number $x$ as input, and it outputs a real number. We can describe this fact using the following notation:\n\n$$\nf: x \\longrightarrow 2x+1\n$$\n\nSimilarly, we can define a function $\\mathbf T,$ also called a **transformation** or a **map**, that takes a 2D-vector (or 3D-vector) as input and outputs a new 2D-vector (or, respectively, 3D-vector). \n\nFor example, let's consider the following transformation: \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThis means that for any 2D-vector $\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}$ the corresponding image $\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}$ under the action of $\\mathbf{T}$ can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWe can evaluate this transformation just like we would with any other function. For example, applying the transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ to the input vector \n$\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}$\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1+3 \\\\ 2\\cdot 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe say that the transformation $\\mathbf T$ *maps* the input vector $\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$ to the output vector $\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}$" :tutorial/id #uuid "58dc3c80-54e0-549f-afc1-e5a3b8cbea52" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3525 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "b716871b-bb81-5bf2-8223-80c9510b7921" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088637}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088603 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087746 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8c04b23-e341-57e9-a072-985e4b536e5a"} :step/id #uuid "15549c3e-d1ae-52a9-b57f-520764e652b6"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088604 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087747 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ad1c29f7-c0e7-5bed-944f-a2e33579c7b8"} :step/id #uuid "c11e935e-6e42-5053-8e60-e60d238b8a80" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088605}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088605 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087748 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "381f7ffe-ae4b-5e45-9fa9-e2a6bd8348b3"} :step/id #uuid "b01168ef-ba36-595a-90db-36c9c6fc6b90" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088606}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088606 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087749 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9fbd335c-28cc-5f02-b773-f685e8b15417"} :step/id #uuid "8f470406-9e89-58e2-bd83-097c8b921250" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088603}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088637 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088940 :tutorial/content "A transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ is called a **linear transformation** (or **linear map**) if the following two properties are satisfied:\n\n- $\\mathbf{T}(k\\mathbf{v})=k\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v})$ for any vector $\\mathbf{v}$ and any scalar $k$\n\n- $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v}_1+\\mathbf{v}_2)=\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v}_1)+\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v}_2)$ for any vectors $\\mathbf{v}_1$ and $\\mathbf{v}_2$\n\nIf we let $\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}$ $\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}$ $\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$ then the conditions above can be written as follows:\n\n- $\\begin{bmatrix}kx \\\\ ky\\end{bmatrix}$\n\n- $\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nWe can determine whether the transformation $\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}$ is linear by checking if these two conditions are true.\n\n- Checking the first condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\begin{bmatrix}kx \\\\ ky\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}(kx)+(ky) \\\\ 2(ky)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}k(x+y) \\\\ k(2y)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =k\\begin{bmatrix}x+y \\\\ 2y\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =kT\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Checking the second condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2})+({y}_{1}+{y}_{2}) \\\\ 2({y}_{1}+{y}_{2})\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}({x}_{1}+{y}_{1})+({x}_{2}+{y}_{2}) \\\\ 2{y}_{1}+2{y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+{y}_{1} \\\\ 2{y}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2}+{y}_{2} \\\\ 2{y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBoth conditions are satisfied, so this transformation is linear." :tutorial/id #uuid "5951013b-06e0-5923-bbd4-d8440d67679e" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3935 :tutorial/title "Linear Transformations"} :step/id #uuid "e84e1380-e6a4-5d10-9efe-3491fa692281" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088604}}] :activity/title "Introduction to Linear Transformations" :activity/type {:db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087932}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186048459 :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087746 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087562 :question/id #uuid "07d823d0-39f8-5d70-8df4-7fd15783e148" :question/math-academy-id "e-5427" :question/problem "Are the following transformations linear?\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ satisfies two properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & T\\begin{bmatrix}kx \\\\ ky\\end{bmatrix}=kT\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}, \\\\  & T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's consider $\\mathbf{T}_1.$ Checking the first condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}kx \\\\ ky\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}(kx)^{2} \\\\ (kx)(ky)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{k}^{2}{x}^{2} \\\\ {k}^{2}xy\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =k\\begin{bmatrix}k{x}^{2} \\\\ kxy\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne k{T}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\textbf{T}_1$ is not a linear transformation.\n\nNow, let's consider $\\mathbf{T}_2.$\n\n- Checking the first condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}kx \\\\ ky\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3kx \\\\ kx+2ky\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}k(3x) \\\\ k(x+2y)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =k\\begin{bmatrix}3x \\\\ x+2y\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =k{T}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Checking the second condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}) \\\\ ({x}_{1}+{x}_{2})+2({y}_{1}+{y}_{2})\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} \\\\ ({x}_{1}+2{y}_{1})+({x}_{2}+2{y}_{2})\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{y}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}+2{y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={T}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+{T}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\textbf{T}_2$ is a linear transformation."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8c04b23-e341-57e9-a072-985e4b536e5a" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087995 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "805617c9-a8c4-59a3-be62-a47fc477ffd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084705} {:answer/id #uuid "9be54c22-8f8d-5207-aca2-2613d0f04c04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084706} {:answer/id #uuid "d97cecb1-de2a-5f51-a2d3-8b44939b8b69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084707} {:answer/id #uuid "22ed53c4-84a1-50dd-8cc0-06dc752357a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084708} {:answer/id #uuid "428ff64d-dbe8-548e-9efe-2a1565e0d916" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084709}] :answer-field/id #uuid "bbd9c0c9-ceec-5c81-8128-c630f394ddde" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084704}] :question/id #uuid "0f56867b-44b5-5e54-8a65-515646e8e908" :question/math-academy-id "q-12010" :question/problem "Let\n$T: \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}x^{2} + y^{2} \\\\ 2x + 7y\\end{bmatrix}$.\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $T(kv) = kT(v)$ for any real $2 \\cdot 1$ column vector $v$ and real scalar $k$\n2. $T(v_{1} + v_{2}) = T(v_{1}) + T(v_{2})$ for any real $2 \\cdot 1$ column vectors $v_{1}$ and $v_{2}$\n3. $T$ is **NOT** a linear transformation"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088417 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed20dcfb-93aa-5edf-8467-1766b4b4b822" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477473} {:answer/id #uuid "d32af6f8-8b0f-5234-806c-62e9d747df5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477474}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477474} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c20384a-0816-5afd-a2d2-3cd169248491" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477706} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93078b9b-9d6c-5f09-8800-51a8a1ec8bbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477475} {:answer/id #uuid "2ea56d0c-ed1c-5b1a-8bbd-91e911ada20d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477476}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477476} :answer-field/id #uuid "fdecd740-b0ed-58be-95a9-c0e256d73db9" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477707} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4df3c9b-0f75-5bb2-b7f3-076984d785f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477477} {:answer/id #uuid "f15219cd-4112-5f94-bd53-1aa374fbf965" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477478}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477478} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c819544-8a99-529a-8823-7309e6fe05a9" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477708}] :question/id #uuid "a9a96319-3bb3-5dd4-a3ac-27f5effab07d" :question/math-academy-id "q-8331" :question/problem "Let \n$T:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}y \\\\ x\\end{bmatrix}.$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $T(kv)=kT(v)$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vector $v$ and real scalar $k$\nII. $T({v}_{1}+{v}_{2})=T({v}_{1})+T({v}_{2})$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$\nIII. $T$ is a linear transformation\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A linear transformation $T$ satisfies two properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & T\\begin{bmatrix}kx \\\\ ky\\end{bmatrix}=kT\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}, \\\\  & T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Checking the first condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\begin{bmatrix}kx \\\\ ky\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}ky \\\\ kx\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =k\\begin{bmatrix}y \\\\ x\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =kT\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Checking the second condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{T}$ is a linear transformation.\n\nAs a result, all three statements are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253648 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "533214b3-6c61-52ee-85dd-a8d6006ced54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461917} {:answer/id #uuid "23c15b20-858c-5295-90c6-68f113ba9d04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461918}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461917} :answer-field/id #uuid "52121635-762f-5923-b01d-1582f7ea794d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462712} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7d6c812-7ee3-5e26-b033-2a4ef6caab4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461919} {:answer/id #uuid "eba0a9bc-d740-58d4-9682-e24f2ebd01d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461920}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461919} :answer-field/id #uuid "b222fe66-ffd9-5e28-8684-edf53b486030" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462713} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1921f4a9-2a50-5748-bfbb-ee6ebd7a5229" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461921} {:answer/id #uuid "2feb6598-cea3-599a-adb9-4e0e897d27ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461922}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461922} :answer-field/id #uuid "79c1742e-b505-51ed-b84e-0e730cf0b35e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462714}] :question/id #uuid "a3a19c98-b506-54b2-aa6b-86aada819468" :question/math-academy-id "q-12012" :question/problem "Let \n$T:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}{x}^{2} \\\\ 7y\\end{bmatrix}.$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $T(kv)=kT(v)$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vector $v$ and real scalar $k$\n- **II.** $T({v}_{1}+{v}_{2})=T({v}_{1})+T({v}_{2})$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$\n- **III.** $T$ is **NOT** a linear transformation\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A linear transformation $T$ satisfies two properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & T\\begin{bmatrix}kx \\\\ ky\\end{bmatrix}=kT\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}, \\\\  & T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Checking the first condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\begin{bmatrix}kx \\\\ ky\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}(kx)^{2} \\\\ 7(ky)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{k}^{2}({x}^{2}) \\\\ k(7y)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =k\\begin{bmatrix}k({x}^{2}) \\\\ 7y\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne kT\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{T}$ is not a linear transformation.\n\n- Checking the second condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2})^{2} \\\\ 7({y}_{1}+{y}_{2})\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2} \\\\ 7{y}_{1}+7{y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}^{2} \\\\ 7{y}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\ 7{y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2{x}_{1}{x}_{2} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2{x}_{1}{x}_{2} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, only statement III is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284660 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bfd51e38-d92a-5e3f-9610-a20858760152" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465591} {:answer/id #uuid "31ed2499-deea-54d0-8415-eeb248c8c543" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465592}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465592} :answer-field/id #uuid "b686b9cb-12bd-5580-a6e3-c47ab3efa6d0" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466639} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2869bddc-de10-5721-9441-0bb4e2ab4217" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465593} {:answer/id #uuid "2cd2be40-511a-5bde-a15d-59a03b250eb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465594}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465594} :answer-field/id #uuid "54aba0a8-32f5-5c3a-8806-6ed7d2edb832" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466640} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b56c6ca-9473-5257-a023-177a68fb22d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465595} {:answer/id #uuid "0086d823-0762-5efc-9a6b-688329e0ad7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465596}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465596} :answer-field/id #uuid "40045fdb-0450-5edc-9f5f-4aa6e6175f96" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466641}] :question/id #uuid "392b472a-8eb5-510e-870b-90564b90ad03" :question/math-academy-id "q-170638" :question/problem "Let \n$T:\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}x+y \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $T(kv)=kT(v)$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vector $v$ and real scalar $k$\n\nII. $T({v}_{1}+{v}_{2})=T({v}_{1})+T({v}_{2})$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$\n\nIII. $T$ is a linear transformation\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A linear transformation $T$ satisfies two properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & T\\begin{bmatrix}kx \\\\ ky\\end{bmatrix}=kT\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}, \\\\  & T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Checking the first condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\begin{bmatrix}kx \\\\ ky\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}kx+ky \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}k(x+y) \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =k\\begin{bmatrix}x+y \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =kT\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Checking the second condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}({x}_{1}+{x}_{2})+({y}_{1}+{y}_{2}) \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}({x}_{1}+{y}_{1})+({x}_{2}+{y}_{2}) \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+{y}_{1} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2}+{y}_{2} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+T\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{T}$ is a linear transformation.\n\nAs a result, all three statements are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284661 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f7e2b7e-e309-5a7f-bd15-1dc1b4f018b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465597} {:answer/id #uuid "1bd65821-b67f-5f1e-bfd9-730d7932bbeb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465598}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465597} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b34043b-63f9-5fa0-a22b-0f554e482772" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466642} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e85b11b-9116-5803-b998-326a84d0a854" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465599} {:answer/id #uuid "ef9a180e-d1f1-5448-8cfe-21b6fb5e12c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465600}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :a