                       \n                                        \n                                        $T(q)=\\,⟨$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-3}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(kq+hr)=T(kq)+T(hr)=kT(q)+hT(r)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor any vectors $q$ and $r.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(3q+r) & =3T(q)+T(r) \\\\ ⟨10,17,9⟩ & =3T(q)+⟨-8,17,3⟩ \\\\ 3T(q) & =⟨10,17,9⟩-⟨-8,17,3⟩ \\\\ 3T(q) & =⟨18,0,6⟩ \\\\ T(q) & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨18,0,6⟩ \\\\ T(q) & =⟨6,0,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292877 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82fa39fa-d638-5008-9c08-aedaac44bbdf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291185}] :ans