ue of $det(D)?$" :question/worked-solution "The row operation applied to $C$ consists of multiplying a row by the number $\\frac{8}{21}.$\n\nWhen we do this, the determinant is multiplied by the same number. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(D) & =\\frac{8}{21}det(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{21}\\cdot (-126) \\\\  & =-48.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265963 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "286e6c23-07b7-5545-a441-9b04e008b90e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263350} {:answer/id #uuid "4c6428b7-cec3-5983-8fd4-6d5bfd014e11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263662} {:answer/id #uuid "4f2b9105-1dc5-57ef-87e1-d54b08b77a89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263689} {:answer/id #uuid "d25edb74-8a68-5d7d-8761-5cc2ad370bc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264834} {:answer/id #uuid "f485bfa8-3aea-5a28-ac04-0ce06bbcbe24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265146}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263350} :answer-field/id #uuid "83755a28-ab8b-5aef-9021-ec305e4c871e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265479}] :question/id #uuid "e4a32b49-da98-512a-a647-8bab7fd6db7d" :question/math-academy-id "q-130732" :question/problem "Suppose $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $det(A)=-63.$ The matrix $B$ is obtained from $A$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{3}:=\\frac{2}{9}{R}_{3}.$ What is the value of $det(B)?$" :question/worked-solution "The row operation applied to $A$ consists of multiplying a row by the number $\\frac{2}{9}.$\n\nWhen we do this, the determinant is multiplied by the same number. So, we have\n\n$$\n