\\cdot (-det(B)) \\\\  & =-2det(B) \\\\  & =-2\\cdot (-7) \\\\  & =14.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411966 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40238690-4089-5383-b0be-144e4a66318a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411917} {:answer/id #uuid "40a285bb-2c28-5dc2-bb55-500bf985bb7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411918} {:answer/id #uuid "43e91860-50ac-5b66-b967-946f1e1fc8f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411921} {:answer/id #uuid "6a51c6b8-2c73-55e3-a6ed-302213e3f577" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411925} {:answer/id #uuid "bae51b38-f76c-5484-acc5-93c339e8b199" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411940}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411918} :answer-field/id #uuid "31de2b36-2a3a-5de3-9428-2467d57745e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411955}] :question/id #uuid "8e473584-e9d3-56ba-b273-e8476acf9443" :question/math-academy-id "q-72750" :question/problem "Suppose $C$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and $det(C)=-24.$ The matrix $D$ is obtained from $C$ by applying the elementary row operations ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{5}$ and ${R}_{3}:=-\\frac{1}{6}{R}_{3}.$ What is the value of $det(D)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's figure out what each operation does to the determinant.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{5}$ involves swapping two rows, so it changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite one.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{3}:=-\\frac{1}{6}{R}_{3}$ involves multiplying a row by $-\\frac{1}{6},$ so the determinant is multiplied by $-\\frac{1}{6}$ as well.\n\nTherefore, we have to change the sign of the determinant to the opposite one and multiply by $-\\frac{1}{6}$ as well. Consequently, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(D) & =-\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot (-det(C)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}det(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot (-24) \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440484 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "017c23cc-c363-5c6e-87b5-6e7c3ae5e977" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440472} {:answer/id #uuid "0d4fda87-7e6e-55cf-a40d-16eb860dbe92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440474} {:answer/id #uuid "81b440ea-43a7-5db4-bd71-d49d81ed4b25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440477} {:answer/id #uuid "b26eabf3-1144-53cd-932b-1525e01f62fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "90" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440479} {:answer/id #uuid "fd7979e9-0f01-5714-b611-2b2303ead7b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440481}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440474} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1483cc5-4c9b-5aca-8098-5a910582cb85" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440483}] :question/id #uuid "ba8abd45-3c22-5be5-a8a7-0f2c616dbcc7" :question/math-academy-id "q-130770" :question/problem "Suppose $Y$ is a $9\\times 9$ matrix and $det(Y)=75.$ The matrix $Z$ is obtained from $Y$ by applying the elementary row operations ${R}_{8}↔{R}_{9}$ and ${R}_{7}:={R}_{7}+\\frac{2}{5}{R}_{2}.$ What is the value of $det(Z)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's figure out what each operation does to the determinant.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{8}↔{R}_{9}$ involves swapping two rows, so it changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite one.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{7}:={R}_{7}+\\frac{2}{5}{R}_{2}$ involves adding a multiple of one row to another row,  so it does not change the determinant.\n\nTherefore, we only have to change the sign of the determinant to the opposite one. Consequently, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Z) & =-det(Y) \\\\  & =-(75) \\\\  & =-75.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498488 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33b25027-8221-5098-9167-254d753c3213" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497909} {:answer/id #uuid "4f11998a-ad24-5209-8a9f-c63c403858e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497989} {:answer/id #uuid "5bda7aff-8f4a-54a5-aebf-3a9be4dd94f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498017} {:answer/id #uuid "9a175c4f-3333-5a30-a0ee-942d881a95f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498148} {:answer/id #uuid "cb8dc81a-a234-558b-87aa-921ac69d0c23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498254}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498017} :answer-field/id #uuid "594aa2c5-6ab3-59e0-94ef-12b55bd75a5d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498398}] :question/id #uuid "023c52b0-f119-5895-8d3f-31a9468a20b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-130768" :question/problem "Suppose $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and $det(A)=6.$ The matrix $B$ is obtained from $A$ by applying the elementary row operations ${R}_{2}↔{R}_{3}$ and ${R}_{3}:=4{R}_{3}.$ What is the value of $det(B)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's figure out what each operation does to the determinant.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}↔{R}_{3}$ involves swapping two rows, so it changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite one.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{3}:=4{R}_{3}$ involves multiplying a row by $4,$ so the determinant is multiplied by $4$ as well.\n\nTherefore, we have to change the sign of the determinant to the opposite one and multiply by $4$ as well. Consequently, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =4\\cdot (-det(A)) \\\\  & =-4det(A) \\\\  & =-4\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =-24.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Determinant After Applying Several Elementary Operations"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119850 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119665 :question/id #uuid "cbd9b4bc-146a-57f7-a03f-f045f86f3c21" :question/math-academy-id "e-6143" :question/problem "Given that $\\det(X)=\\det(Y),$ which elementary row operations transforms matrix $X$ to matrix $Y,$ where\n\n![](images/38/3813c34b623ef9ad6f7ca534fb3a6e373d4ce1961dab49dfab9e414fea84daae.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Since $\\det(X)=\\det(Y)$, the row operation applied to $X$ must be to add or subtract a multiple of one row to another row. In other words, it is of the form \n\n$$\nR_j := R_j + (k)R_i, \\quad i \\neq j.\n$$\n\nBy considering the given row operations that are of the above form, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(X) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{3} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =det(Y).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\nR_2:= R_2 + 3R_3.\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9a0ab53e-79ff-5520-bb50-069fd381d29d" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120420 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37511006-3cc1-5044-a452-04788f70a6b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324422} {:answer/id #uuid "52ff4a1e-e084-5b7a-9da2-3d3878cd71ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}↔{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324653} {:answer/id #uuid "71e11479-c1c3-5398-9ce8-e2748445bd42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324913} {:answer/id #uuid "9d025d13-dbb9-5f4d-81e6-a2fb2be38c43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325304} {:answer/id #uuid "c5d34638-1f12-5d11-897f-c363aca5a5d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325677}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325304} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa554bb6-6241-52a2-a8a6-09b04c9e8078" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326528}] :question/id #uuid "1d4250d6-4c9c-5a2c-ac92-71ea5c8419b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-42076" :question/problem "Given that $det(A)=det(B),$ which of the following elementary row operations transforms matrix $A$ to matrix $B,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since $det(A)=det(B)$, the row operation applied to $A$ must be to add or subtract a multiple of one row to another row. In other words, it is of the form \n\n$$\n{R}_{j}:={R}_{j}+(k){R}_{i},\\,i\\ne j.\n$$\n\nBy considering the given row operations that are of the above form, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =det(B).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120456 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32f10a65-b2dd-5264-be04-cd77ee8486f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385462} {:answer/id #uuid "a32db1a3-8910-58f3-addd-697a1c8eac50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385463} {:answer/id #uuid "ca1e7385-be8c-569c-a83a-fd9c19722762" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385464} {:answer/id #uuid "d3ea8a4a-610c-59b9-b2ef-b66f8acee455" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385465} {:answer/id #uuid "43d84a56-269f-58a8-93a2-b0ccafcfa0f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385466}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385463} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ccd8d0e-7322-5ccb-9755-abded82540db" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385461}] :question/id #uuid "fd213cdd-f67a-5a57-9e3f-84846a552cf7" :question/math-academy-id "q-43080" :question/problem "Consider the matrices given below. Given that $X$ and $Y$ are row equivalent matrices and $det(X)=-8$, find $det(Y).$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,Y=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $Y$ can be obtained from $X$ by swapping the $2$nd and the $3$rd rows. \n\nThis changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite one.\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Y) & =-det(X) \\\\  & =-(-8) \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265985 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36d8f1dd-9c61-582a-91cb-1b1b14e544ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263489} {:answer/id #uuid "7cfe718c-c4c1-5e05-a605-9f1eeeec4a53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264078} {:answer/id #uuid "b62d6a25-1160-5e5d-826d-11092cfa8fd1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264579} {:answer/id #uuid "ee61c6e2-7ebd-5d28-8d0e-3007260e4c30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265084} {:answer/id #uuid "f1a2f26a-317b-5119-9e11-1fcf1b2dfd40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=2{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265123}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263489} :answer-field/id #uuid "eab97c28-5a65-571d-9829-1e7bb5397bea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265662}] :question/id #uuid "7d54eadd-5171-5d74-9872-72cd2ba1ef45" :question/math-academy-id "q-130843" :question/problem "Given that $det(A)=det(B),$ which of the following elementary row operations transforms matrix $A$ to matrix $B,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 8 & -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -8\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since $det(A)=det(B)$, the row operation applied to $A$ must be to add or subtract a multiple of one row to another row. In other words, it is of the form \n\n$$\n{R}_{j}:={R}_{j}+(k){R}_{i},\\,i\\ne j.\n$$\n\nBy considering the given row operations that are of the above form, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 8 & -2\\end{aligned}| & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =det(B).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265992 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f938576-14ee-5665-942c-f5bfc3534050" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263289} {:answer/id #uuid "66e265c6-ed48-5d88-966e-a5dff8678916" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:=-{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263892} {:answer/id #uuid "96934c85-fbb8-5687-a238-dbee446961d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264288} {:answer/id #uuid "a3c6c16d-b28c-5665-bfd2-d38f6dbf5091" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264392} {:answer/id #uuid "d5476105-e8e0-591e-9f16-19d7dff3433b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264857}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264392} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d92ecd7-28e6-5f20-bfc3-d836c30d39c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265497}] :question/id #uuid "a88eab2f-0bec-591e-a119-0d1e91654bf5" :question/math-academy-id "q-130854" :question/problem "Given that $det(A)=det(B),$ which of the following elementary row operations transforms matrix $A$ to matrix $B,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since $det(A)=det(B)$, the row operation applied to $A$ must be to add or subtract a multiple of one row to another row. In other words, it is of the form \n\n$$\n{R}_{j}:={R}_{j}+(k){R}_{i},\\,i\\ne j.\n$$\n\nBy considering the given row operations that are of the above form, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}| & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{3} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =det(B).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{3}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265993 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5631a190-3164-5c81-9c22-e6a70c44c09d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263742} {:answer/id #uuid "74e1b546-dc5d-5c39-8615-b03158b816ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264014} {:answer/id #uuid "850ef7c7-1f4b-53c9-b078-25bda4009629" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264145} {:answer/id #uuid "df7141db-3b66-5a7a-b89e-874dcb0bbee8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264937} {:answer/id #uuid "e044d557-77d9-53d0-a554-77b04c1a4a41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264947}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264014} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf6cdcea-ffe0-5e06-a7c5-0284d3815f01" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265614}] :question/id #uuid "2e099506-9b8a-52ad-a7eb-ff6f42b6d002" :question/math-academy-id "q-130855" :question/problem "Consider the matrices given below. Given that $X$ and $Y$ are row equivalent matrices and $det(X)=5$, find $det(Y).$\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,Y=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $Y$ can be