ow operations that are of the above form, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}| & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-3){R}_{3} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & -8 & 10 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =det(B).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-3){R}_{3}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385442 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eef6e93d-f65c-5ac8-a313-118c028fcea5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385444} {:answer/id #uuid "4f761496-d7dc-5eaf-8c5f-a2ed07387580" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385445} {:answer/id #uuid "f1f9e742-6ad1-5201-ab5d-6de6ae61dad2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385446} {:answer/id #uuid "c17d0592-c56f-54f6-b24a-c443443b36de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385447} {:answer/id #uuid "c02317d2-d147-540e-940b-ea20052b0ef4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385448}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385447} :answer-field/id #uuid "36b4251d-aea0-541f-9df1-43c7caac3dd1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385443}] :question/id #uuid "6f2538da-8d51-59ef-9c88-dd06d7af1438" :question/math-academy-id "q-43047" :question/problem "Given that $det(A)=det(B),$ which of the following elementary row operations transforms matrix $A$ to matrix $B,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since $det(A)=det(B)$, the row operation applied to $A$ must be to add or subtract a multiple of one row to another row. In other words, it is of the form \n\n$$\n{R}_{j}:={R}_{j}+(k){R}_{i},\\,i\\ne j.\n$$\n\nBy considering the given row operations that are of the above form, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{3} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =det(B).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{3}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409690 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f5903e6-2dfb-5988-91aa-d76353ccd959" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409659} {:answer/id #uuid "6d3a3be9-dab5-5f7f-8e95-4eab3b47ad8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}↔{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409665} {:answer/id #uuid "6d7bf72b-a934-51fa-b417-3e7f04a3f3b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409666} {:answer/id #uuid "7190fbd3-e0c2-5f59-a1f5-3e49c40c46d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:=2{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409668} {:answer/id #uuid "c8afe3f3-a5ef-55a7-b5dd-30e21d2e58fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409676}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409659} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a779adf-221a-5189-a14f-312c86e15c0d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409685}] :question/id #uuid "9ac571f6-6f05-5f70-8bcf-34738f544556" :question/math-academy-id "q-43046" :question/problem "Given that $det(A)=det(B),$ which of the following elementary row operations transforms matrix $A$ to matrix $B,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 5 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 1\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since $det(A)=det(B)$, the row operation applied to $A$ must be to add or subtract a multiple of one row to another row. In other words, it is of the form \n\n$$\n{R}_{j}:={R}_{j}+(k){R}_{i},\\,i\\ne j.\n$$\n\nBy considering the given row operations that are of the above form, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 5 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 1\\end{aligned}| & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =det(B).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411963 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1efd96de-5d59-5c21-b6c4-f57a804edb99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411913} {:answer/id #uuid "2bb7ef99-5504-5559-a251-067d58c0bd0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411914} {:answer/id #uuid "5f7847c9-3225-566d-a4bb-dbc66736309d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411923} {:answer/id #uuid "ca4dd63f-7252-5bf2-9499-144f36222c27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411945} {:answer/id #uuid "e1001e71-dfc2-59ca-a3c7-8d9e00835d22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411947}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411945} :answer-field/id #uuid "93fee275-10ef-55f5-b6b3-8793339d38c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411961}] :question/id #uuid "441df1fa-6b02-5f85-abd1-1592ef6dada4" :question/math-academy-id "q-72770" :question/problem "Consider the matrices given below. Given that $A$ and $B$ are row equivalent matrices and $det(A)=1$, find $det(B).$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -8 & 12 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $B$ can be obtained from $A$ by multiplying the $2$nd row by $4.$ \n\nSo, the determinant is multiplied by $4$ as well.\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =4\\cdot det(A) \\\\  & =4\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424899 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "171230a8-065f-5312-91ff-166c6fb3df4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424893} {:answer/id #uuid "21bc26a0-57ad-5e62-a6e6-621e2ba24583" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424894} {:answer/id #uuid "54d72f80-7a7b-5b93-a0ec-2d6edad08ac4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424895} {:answer/id #uuid "6c11e90f-184e-57bd-b3ed-1971d8fb82ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=-{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424896} {:answer/id #uuid "acde6755-f2db-5c6c-bdc1-ac03bdaa2931" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424897}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424894} :answer-field/id #uuid "c75bea69-7db0-5820-97b1-b5dd95b8b845" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424898}] :question/id #uuid "200dace6-387b-586f-87ab-a5501c01cbe0" :question/math-academy-id "q-130851" :question/problem "Given that $det(A)=det(B),$ which of the following elementary row operations transforms matrix $A$ to matrix $B,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since $det(A)=det(B)$, the row operation applied to $A$ must be to add or subtract a multiple of one row to another row. In other words, it is of the form \n\n$$\n{R}_{j}:={R}_{j}+(k){R}_{i},\\,i\\ne j.\n$$\n\nBy considering the given row operations that are of the above form, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 5\\end{aligned}| & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =det(B).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483371 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56f3cc0b-c41a-5321-9ece-52fd3df64297" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482965} {:answer/id #uuid "6f6d1a51-1150-5aa3-a923-b68b4f05b638" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483003} {:answer/id #uuid "704a8b44-8729-5565-b1a0-2928425f981b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483007} {:answer/id #uuid "c19dca01-b95f-5b0c-9166-3c0789c3ce6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483137} {:answer/id #uuid "ffcdefc7-8d2b-5c46-b8de-33fa51d9e81e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483241}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483137} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd91fbcc-9a1e-515e-941d-2e16f7668942" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483318}] :question/id #uuid "5c8f03a1-964a-5fd4-a60f-a2aa229186e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-43048" :question/problem "Consider the matrices given below. Given that $A$ and $B$ are row equivalent matrices and $det(A)=6$, find $det(B).$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -5 & 6 & 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 6 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $B$ can be obtained from $A$ by swapping the $2$nd and the $3$rd rows. \n\nThis changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite one.\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =-det(A) \\\\  & =-(6) \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Row Operation Given the Connection Between Two Determinants"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119851 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119666 :question/id #uuid "ce910ef2-c3af-5173-84d4-ee2a4c957954" :question/math-academy-id "e-6148" :question/problem "Suppose $A$ is a $4\\times4$ matrix and $\\det(A)=5.$ What is the value of $\\det(2A)?$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying a $n\\times n$ matrix by a scalar $k$ is equivalent to multiplying each row by $k,$ and this occurs $n$ times. This leads to the result\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(k\\cdot A)={k}^{n}\\cdot det(A).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $k=2$ and $n=4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(2A) & ={2}^{4}\\cdot det(A) \\\\  & =16\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =80.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "272d9a54-ba97-5175-86df-0a78337da7b9" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120512 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8abf4f46-cb92-54d4-9c70-8a06f7b21b34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119187} {:answer/id #uuid "b754331f-0621-514f-bb21-c33b15a5df9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119188} {:answer/id #uuid "d19fa999-5542-53c5-93ad-fb03f8d1b1df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "180" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119189} {:answer/id #uuid "f3b57cea-9992-5113-b6bb-b7cd9b529ae9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119190} {:answer/id #uuid "7056a792-6c7c-55a8-ae98-5119231757b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "500" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119191}] :answer-field/id #uuid "96d753a8-f1b5-5349-8713-466168c43148" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119186}] :question/id #uuid "f286d370-93a2-57ee-8818-1b6a7ccd9ac3" :question/math-academy-id "q-72462" :question/problem "Suppose $A$ is a $3 \\cdot 3$ matrix and $det(A) = 4$. What is the value of $det(5A)$?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120513 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b13947d-94d2-558e-a909-cf932f9ace0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336136} {:answer/id #uuid "1047b1d9-9b78-55e6-9cc9-ddeaf7c22b05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336184} {:answer/id #uuid "d9df1ef5-dea4-5f58-bb7d-2c73082ae731" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337928} {:answer/id #uuid "dc9e2c4f-0ea5-5364-9c0b-8745a2456641" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "54" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337950} {:answer/id #uuid "dfb68948-e6ba-52f3-86ef-0c4cc638e42a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 175921863379