-130737" :question/problem "Suppose $C$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $det(C)=-5.$ What is the value of $det(-2C)?$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying a $n\\times n$ matrix by a scalar $k$ is equivalent to multiplying each row by $k,$ and this occurs $n$ times. This leads to the result\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(k\\cdot C)={k}^{n}\\cdot det(C).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $k=-2$ and $n=4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(-2C) & =(-2)^{4}\\cdot det(C) \\\\  & =16\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =-80.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409689 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "512abaff-433d-5e4a-864f-f1df10d56d6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409663} {:answer/id #uuid "7a56edfe-4461-57d1-8804-22f3e005401a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409670} {:answer/id #uuid "f689939f-47fe-5c00-a125-9fe1fc1187ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "180" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409679} {:answer/id #uuid "face2d4d-2a2b-5eb7-8047-8fb6dbd54d8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "160" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409680} {:answer/id #uuid "fcf8031f-e31a-5703-96b3-5a28bec971aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "320" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409682}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "320" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409682} :answer-field/id #uuid "98c176ba-da66-551c-9c0c-0c257e4d9459" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409686}] :question/id #uuid "81c5993c-3d71-5869-bbf5-3e36b2df3a7f" :question/math-academy-id "q-72741" :question/problem "Suppose $Y$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $det(Y)=5.$ What is the value of $det(2Y)?$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying a $n\\times n$ matrix by a scalar $k$ is equivalent to multiplying each row by $k,$ and this occurs $n$ times. This leads to the result\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(k\\cdot Y)={k}^{n}\\cdot det(Y).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $k=2$ and $n=6.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(2Y) & ={2}^{6}\\cdot det(Y) \\\\  & =64\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =320.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409691 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08098a6b-f06b-51d7-be19-39ddeb566f21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-256" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409658} {:answer/id #uuid "4da115ec-321e-53f5-9c9a-06b3818508a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409661} {:answer/id #uuid "7105bb69-b089-5e84-ab20-fd40c1edbdff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-864" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409667} {:answer/id #uuid "b58e6bc8-29ce-5a41-8721-675b80eb22cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-144" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409673} {:answer/id #uuid "fcd30542-3cc5-5b61-a9af-49753027f933" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409681}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-144" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409673} :answer-field/id #uuid "04759499-638f-5548-ad9a-51762b698235" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409683}] :question/id #uuid "fded0a2c-cd1a-5de1-a671-20ea991daecd" :question/math-academy-id "q-72737" :question/problem "Suppose $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix and $det(A)=-4.$ What is the value of $det(6A)?$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying a $n\\times n$ matrix by a scalar $k$ is equivalent to multiplying each row by $k,$ and this occurs $n$ times. This leads to the result\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(k\\cdot A)={k}^{n}\\cdot det(A).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $k=6$ and $n=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(6A) & ={6}^{2}\\cdot det(A) \\\\  & =36\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =-144.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440485 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09a794be-72e1-5850-a9e7-4f09532bb4d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440473} {:answer/id #uuid "2c9a3462-424a-5e23-93a1-21351e2c8529" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-384" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440475} {:answer/id #uuid "3aad9ad4-b303-5b2b-9d26-6d2c4b559298" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440476} {:answer/id #uuid "8a223201-44a6-5017-aa80-a127d44a8e76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-147" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440478} {:answer/id #uuid "c00986c8-2ab1-5ba7-aed5-8ac51531c5fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-294" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440480}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-147" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440478} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad94b206-3ccb-5817-8ec1-05230e22359f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440482}] :question/id #uuid "fc497788-364d-5c29-8657-a4f1556e2704" :question/math-academy-id "q-72744" :question/problem "Suppose $X$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix and $det(X)=-3.$ What is the value of $det(7X)?$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying a $n\\times n$ matrix by a scalar $k$ is equivalent to multiplying each row by $k,$ and this occurs $n$ times. This leads to the result\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(k\\cdot X)={k}^{n}\\cdot det(X).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $k=7$ and $n=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(7X) & ={7}^{2}\\cdot det(X) \\\\  & =49\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =-147.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Determinant After Multiplying a Matrix by a Scalar"}] :topic/math-academy-id 1772 :topic/title "Row and Column Operations on Determinants"}]}
